From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:24:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wsi: Haiku views present on the GPU, straight to the screen
 in direct mode

Swapchains for a Haiku view use the GPU's own images and copy each
present out on the present queue: into the screen's frame buffer
(imported as a dma-buf), clipped to what the BDirectWindow reports
through vkDirectConnectedHAIKU, or else into a staging buffer that goes
to the view as a bitmap. FIFO waits for the vertical blank.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
